  "description": "Certificate of Lawful Development (Proposed): Change of Use from residential dwelling (Class C3) to a residential children's home (Class C2) for up to four children and two staff",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed change of use from Dwelling (Class C3A) to Children’s Home (Class C2) would not fall within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 3 of the General Permitted Development Order (2015) (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;It has not been demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority that the use or operations described in the application would be lawful within the meaning of S192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) if instituted or begun at the time of the application. Specifically, the application fails to demonstrate whether the proposals would not form a material change of use and in the absence of compelling evidence, Officers cannot conclude otherwise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
